WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.210
After a couple of big-screen appearances,
Jason Momoa's Aquaman is finally stepping

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.900
out on his own with his first solo adventure.

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:12.740
Whether you're a longtime comics reader or
completely unfamiliar with this classic character's

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.080
legacy, here's everything you need to know
before seeing Aquaman.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:22.480
Aquaman wasn't always a sea-based superhero
— he was born Arthur Curry, a half-Atlantean,

00:00:22.499 --> 00:00:26.489
half-human boy whose mother Queen Atlanna
was forced to leave him in the care of his

00:00:26.489 --> 00:00:28.100
human father, Thomas Curry.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.680
However, in being split between these two
worlds, Arthur is rejected by both sides of

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.160
his heritage, and in the end, he finds himself
somewhat lost.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.180
"I just feel like I never really embraced
the sea or the land.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.140
I've been a loner my whole life."

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.660
As an adult, Arthur must find his place in
both worlds, vie for his right to become king

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.220
of Atlantis, and protect the world at large.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:54.540
Aquaman has a wide range of powers, including
super strength, extreme durability, the ability

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.440
to breathe underwater, and the power to control
any undersea lifeforms.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:03.160
Aquaman has been around for a while — his
first appearance came in "More Fun Comics

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.780
#73" in 1941 as a backup character to other
heroes.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:13.179
Aquaman lived on in the back pages of Adventure
Comics and during the 1960s, finally joined

00:01:13.179 --> 00:01:18.460
the Justice League, got his own cartoon series,
and became one of the Super Friends, cementing

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.160
his legacy.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:24.780
Director James Wan has said that his Aquaman
movie is largely inspired by writer Geoff

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:27.610
Johns, who rebooted the character in 2011.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.210
Still, Wan didn't leave the older comics behind.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:34.429
He went through dozens of Aquaman comics from
the past 70 years of source material.

00:01:34.429 --> 00:01:38.709
For fans of the cheesy older comics, don't
worry, because Wan couldn't resist using some

00:01:38.709 --> 00:01:40.040
elements from these eras.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.380
Topo, Aquaman's octopus sidekick, will appear
in the film.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:48.700
Fans were likely surprised to hear about Nicole
Kidman's casting in Aquaman, since she hasn't

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.760
appeared in a superhero film since 1995's
Batman Forever.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:57.940
However, Kidman will be officially joining
the DC Universe as Queen Atlanna, the superhuman

00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:59.020
mother of Aquaman.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:03.680
It's still unclear how faithful the film will
be as far as the original comics are concerned,

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.200
but it looks as if Kidman's story will be
a tragic one.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.200
"Your mother left you to save your life.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.980
You can't imagine how it hurt her, what it
cost her."

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:17.860
Atlanna has been written as an outcast, a
queen, and most importantly, Aquaman's link

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:21.440
to his superhuman heritage and his one connection
to Atlantis.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:26.080
However, she's also been written as a fairly
absent parent, so if this film is including

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.360
Aquaman's family history, audiences may see
some tension between the two.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:35.520
Played by Amber Heard, Mera was first seen
in Justice League to provide backstory for

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:39.090
Aquaman, but her role in Aquaman will be much
more substantial.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:43.140
Director James Wan has remarked that Aquaman
is more like Mera's sidekick.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.340
Once Mera appears on-screen in Aquaman, she's
reportedly in nearly every single scene.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:52.900
It's not hard to guess why Wan chose to focus
on Mera so much, as the character is a powerful

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.580
superhero in her own right.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:58.780
She possesses incredible strength and the
ability to completely control water.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:03.160
It seems as if Mera's origin story has been
changed considerably compared to the original

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:03.720
comics.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:08.280
Though Mera usually hails from an alternate
dimension, Justice League revealed a different

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.840
origin where she was raised by Queen Atlanna
as a war orphan:

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.940
"When my parents fought in the wars, she took
me in."

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.440
Sibling rivalry abounds in superhero films,
and Aquaman will be no exception.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.650
In late 2016, it was announced that Patrick
Wilson had signed on as Aquaman's surly and

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.260
powerful half-brother, Orm.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:32.590
In the comics, Orm is a contender for the
throne of Atlantis and nearly destroys the

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.560
sea in his attempt to claim the crown.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.400
In the film, however, some environmentally-minded
audience members may side more with Orm than

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.720
Aquaman in their central conflict.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:45.980
On The Late Show with Stephen Colbert, Wilson
discussed Orm's motivations:

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:52.300
"My whole thing in the movie is to get back
at the surface world for polluting my oceans,

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.920
our oceans, a little bit of environmental
theme going in there.”

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:59.920
Wilson is no stranger to superhero films,
as he previously appeared in Zack Snyder's

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.900
2009 Watchmen adaptation as Nite Owl.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:08.050
He's also familiar with Aquaman's director,
having appeared in Wan's horror hits Insidious

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:09.140
and The Conjuring.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:14.220
Aquaman has his work cut out for him in the
film — in addition to facing off against

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:18.170
Orm, he'll have to deal with Black Manta,
another villain from the original comics.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:23.070
As a ruthless pirate who will stop at nothing
to destroy Atlantis, Black Manta harbors a

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.160
long-held grudge against the underwater metropolis.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:30.930
He's also a brilliant engineer who designed
a diving suit which gives him super strength,

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:34.320
shoots optic blasts, and allows him to survive
underwater.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:40.140
Wan has been extra quiet regarding Black Manta's
specifics — fans only know that Yahya Abdul-Mateen

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:44.060
II, who appeared on Netflix's The Get Down,
will be playing the villain.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.660
Aquaman has one very well-known power:

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:48.980
"The Aquaman.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.260
I hear you can talk to fish."

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:57.400
This has made Aquaman the subject of many
a joke over the years.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.800
But Wan isn't shying away from this particular
power, and fans can expect Aquaman's fish-telepathy

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.340
to play a big part in the film.

